TEMPORARY diagnostic instrumentation for the cold-launch extension host OOM -- not a real fix, remove once root-caused.

ios-exthost-worker-heap.diff's own comments document that raising
resourceLimits.maxOldGenerationSizeMb (tried 256->512->1024->2048, an 8x
range) made zero measurable difference to the cold-launch OOM's crash
timing (~12-20s after launch, every time) -- strong evidence the heap
ceiling isn't actually the limiting factor for that specific case, and
guessing at yet another number is not a productive next step.

Adds a periodic (1s) heap-stats logger to bootstrap-fork.ts, scoped to
only the extension host entrypoint (VSCODE_ESM_ENTRYPOINT ===
'vs/workbench/api/node/extensionHostProcess', so it doesn't add noise to
the agent host or pty host Workers, neither of which has this problem),
writing to stderr -- which is already piped to the parent process's
node-stdio.log as "<worker><stderr>" lines by the existing
console-forwarding infrastructure, so no new log-capture plumbing is
needed to see the output in a captured simulator-test.yml artifact.

Purely additive and gated to a specific env var value already set only
for the extension host process; no behavior change for any other code
path. Meant to be removed (or converted into a real fix) once a captured
log shows what's actually consuming memory during the one-time
cold-launch path this crash is confined to.

First attempt at this patch failed vscode-reh-web-build.yml's own
tsgo-typecheck for real (run 36025966651):

  src/bootstrap-fork.ts(281,11): error TS2339: Property 'unref' does not
  exist on type 'TimeoutHandle'.

Root cause: this tsconfig includes both Node and DOM lib types, and a
bare `setInterval(...)` call resolves to the DOM lib's overload (which
returns a plain numeric handle with no `.unref()`/`.ref()`), not Node's
`NodeJS.Timeout`. Fixed by importing Node's own `setInterval` explicitly
from `node:timers` instead of relying on ambient global overload
resolution -- matching how this same file already prefers explicit
`node:*` imports (`node:buffer`, `node:crypto`) over bare globals for
exactly this kind of ambiguity.

Index: code-server/lib/vscode/src/bootstrap-fork.ts
===================================================================
--- code-server.orig/lib/vscode/src/bootstrap-fork.ts
+++ code-server/lib/vscode/src/bootstrap-fork.ts
@@ -258,6 +258,35 @@
 	(globalThis as any).crypto = (await import('node:crypto')).webcrypto;
 }

+// iOS DIAGNOSTIC (temporary, not a real fix): the extension host Worker
+// reliably OOMs (ERR_WORKER_OUT_OF_MEMORY) ~12-20s after the very first
+// launch following a fresh install, regardless of how high
+// resourceLimits.maxOldGenerationSizeMb is set (confirmed up to 2048MB
+// making zero difference to crash timing -- see
+// ios-exthost-worker-heap.diff's own comments). That timing-independence
+// means the ceiling isn't the real problem; something is actually
+// allocating a lot during this one-time path. Log heap stats every
+// second via stderr (already piped to the parent's node-stdio.log as
+// "<worker><stderr>" lines) so a real captured log shows what's
+// happening right before the crash, instead of guessing at another
+// heap-size number. Scoped to only the extension host entrypoint to
+// avoid noise on the agent host/pty host Workers, which don't have this
+// problem.
+if (process.env['VSCODE_ESM_ENTRYPOINT'] === 'vs/workbench/api/node/extensionHostProcess') {
+	const v8 = await import('node:v8');
+	// Bare `setInterval` resolves to the DOM lib's overload in this
+	// tsconfig (returning a plain number/TimeoutHandle with no .unref()),
+	// not Node's -- import Node's own timer functions explicitly instead
+	// of relying on ambient overload resolution, matching how this file
+	// already prefers explicit `node:*` imports over bare globals.
+	const { setInterval: nodeSetInterval } = await import('node:timers');
+	nodeSetInterval(() => {
+		const mem = process.memoryUsage();
+		const heap = v8.getHeapStatistics();
+		process.stderr.write(`[iOS-DIAG heap] rss=${(mem.rss / 1048576).toFixed(1)}MB heapUsed=${(mem.heapUsed / 1048576).toFixed(1)}MB heapTotal=${(mem.heapTotal / 1048576).toFixed(1)}MB external=${(mem.external / 1048576).toFixed(1)}MB v8UsedHeap=${(heap.used_heap_size / 1048576).toFixed(1)}MB v8TotalHeap=${(heap.total_heap_size / 1048576).toFixed(1)}MB v8HeapLimit=${(heap.heap_size_limit / 1048576).toFixed(1)}MB\n`);
+	}, 1000).unref();
+}
+
 // Bootstrap ESM
 await bootstrapESM();
